# Playball

Playball is an original football game concept inspired by modern football games, built as a fast browser game and arranged for Android packaging with Capacitor.

## Features
- Original dark football aesthetic
- Single-screen match action
- Keyboard controls
- Score tracking and match clock
- Ready for web deployment and Android wrap

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
npm run dev -- --host
```

Then open the local URL shown by Vite.

## Build for production

```bash
npm run build
```

## Android / Play Store preparation

This repository includes Capacitor config for Android packaging.

```bash
npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/cli
npx cap init Playball com.playball.game
npx cap add android
npx cap copy android
```

Then open the Android project in Android Studio and generate a signed bundle or APK for Play Store deployment.

## Asset note

The icon in `assets/app-icon.svg` is original and not a copy of any commercial football game logo.

## Controls
- Move: W A S D
- Pass / Shoot: Space
- Restart: R
